$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x, y) = x + 2y$. Further, let\n\n$I = ∬_(R)f(x, y)dA$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R$, we have\n$L(f, P) \\le I \\le U(f, P)$,\nwhere $L(f, P)$ and $U(f, P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums, and\n\n$U(f, P) = ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)AAAAAΔx_{i}Δy_{j}$.\n\nWhat expression is missing from the double summation above?" 13194139533398 17592186045585 false] [17592186129428 1071 "Let $R=[0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+2y.$ Further, let \n\n$$\nI={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R,$ we have \n$L(f,P)\\,\\le I\\,\\le U(f,P),$\nwhere $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums, and \n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\n$$\n\nWhat expression is missing from the double summation above?" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186129428 1074 "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $U(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions ${R}_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+2y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+2y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}=f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})={x}_{i}+2{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nand the upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}+2{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${x}_{i}+2{y}_{j}.$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133834 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259718 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133834 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259719 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133834 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259721 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133834 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259722 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133834 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259724 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133837 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259717 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133882 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259491 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133884 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259590 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133884 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259591 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133884 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259592 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133884 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259593 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133886 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259506 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133895 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259492 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133895 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259493 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133895 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259496 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133896 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259594 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133896 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259595 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133896 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259596 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133896 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259597 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133896 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259598 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186133896 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259599 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186