 1071 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ given that  $F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\,i+2y\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+t\\,j$ for $t\\in [1,2].$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186134097 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,y=t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & ={e}^{x}\\,i+2y\\,j \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}\\,i+2t\\,j \\\\  & =t\\,i+2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(t\\,i+2t\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+j) \\\\  & =1+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}1+2t\\,dt \\\\  & ={[t+{t}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =[2+4-(1+1)] \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186152157 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259503 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186152157 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259504 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186152157 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259505 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186152238 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259538 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186152238 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259539 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186152238 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259540 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186157293 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259527 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186157293 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259537 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186157576 1068 #edb/ref 