iemann sums, and \n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\n$$\n\nWhat expression is missing from the double summation above?" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259553 1072 #uuid "4c92a16d-8ec0-5bb7-a1d3-67db8dee714c" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259553 1074 "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $U(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions ${R}_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}=f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=3{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2}\n$$\n\nand the upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(3{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $3{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2}.$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259554 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259068 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259554 1069 "q-123740" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259554 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259554 1071 "Let $R=[-1,2]\\times [-4,-1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=3x-8y+6.$ Further, let \n\n$$\nI={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R,$ we have \n$L(f,P)\\,\\le I\\,\\le U(f,P),$\nwhere $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums, and \n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\n$$\n\nWhat expression is missing from the double summation above?" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259554 1072 #uuid "013aa87f-4dba-5dcd-99b5-80fa5d543721" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259554 1074 "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $U(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions ${R}_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y)=3x-8y+6$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=3x-8y+6$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}=f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})=3{x}_{i}-8{y}_{j-1}+6\n$$\n\nand the upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(3{x}_{i}-8{y}_{j-1}+6)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $3{x}_{i}-8{y}_{j-1}+6.$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259555 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259244 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259555 1069 "q-123741" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259555 1070 #edb/ref 