}+{y}_{j-1}\n$$\n\nand the lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}.$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259557 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259270 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259557 1069 "q-123748" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259557 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259557 1071 "![](images/bf/bff60466ca8abba4fd849c046c02af3a4811279774975fc981cafad91d734ed5.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259557 1072 #uuid "1c63175a-a455-54b8-b784-f9c30e4507e1" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259557 1074 "We notice the following:\n\n- Each vector in our vector field is parallel to the $x$-axis. So, the $j$ and $k$ components of our vector field are zero everywhere. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nK(x,y,z)=-i+j\n$$\n\n- Moreover, each vector in our vector field is pointing in the *negative* $x$-direction, so the $i$ component of our vector field is negative. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=i\n$$\n\n- Finally, we note that each vector in our vector field has the same length, so the $i$ component of our vector field is constant. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nG(x,y,z)=-y\\,i\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $H(x,y,z)=-2\\,i.$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259558 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259097 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259558 1069 "q-123749" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259558 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259558 1071 "![](images/f8/f89653698d9c2bad0c2e6a77d4dad1953a9fd72f89cbfc08fd68aac802acd284.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259558 1072 #uuid "589ce8fd-18ca-5044-bdd6-238376c16f16" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259558 1074 "We notice the following:\n\n- Each vector in our vector field is parallel to the $y$-axis. So, the $i$ and $k$ components of our vector field are zero everywhere. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nH(x,y,z)=i+k,\\,K(x,y,z)=i+{e}^{x}\\,k\n$$\n\n- Moreover, each vector in our vector field is pointing in the *negative* $y$-direction, so the $j$ component of our vector field is negative. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=j\n$$\n\n- Finally, we note that each vector in our vector field has the same length, so the $j$ component of our vector field is constant. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nG(x,y,z)=-{x}^{2}\\,j\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram doesn't correspond to any of the listed vector fields." 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259559 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259325 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259559 1069 "q-123750" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259559 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259559 1071 "![](images/cf/cfc15b6202167211b7d6c0e8f6635dd9e571810d5296a209a4c317350604c4a4.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259559 1072 #uuid "c9c83b42-2a92-533d-be7a-98b1b72e544d" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259559 1074 "We notice the following:\n\n- Each vector in our vector field is parallel to the $x$-axis. So, the $j$ and $k$ components of our vector field are zero everywhere. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nG(x,y,z)=i-j\n$$\n\n- Moreover, each vector in our vector field is pointing in the *positive* $x$-direction, so the $i$ component of our vector field is positive. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=-2\\,i,\\,H(x,y,z)=-\\,i\n$$\n\n- Finally, we note that each vector in our vector field has the same length, so the $i$ component of our vector field is constant. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nK(x,y,z)=-{e}^{y}\\,k\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram doesn't correspond to any of the listed vector fields." 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259560 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259246 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259560 1069 "q-123753" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259560 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259560 1071 "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=1-{t}^{2},\\,\\,\\,y=3t+2,\\,-2\\le t\\le 2,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $a$ | $1$ | $0$ | $c$ |\n| $y$ | $-4$ | $-1$ | $b$ | $5$ | $8$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259560 1072 #uuid "3cac2494-d877-5849-8ad0-9d49fb79c7df" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259560 1074 "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $x=1-{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=1-(-1)^{2}=0.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $y=3t+2.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=3(0)+2=2.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=1-{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=1-(2)^{2}=-3.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0+2+(-3)=-1.\n$$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259561 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259251 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259561 1069 "q-123755" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259561 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259561 1071 "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=4t,\\,\\,\\,y=-{t}^{3},\\,-3\\le t\\le 1,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-12$ | $-8$ | $a$ | $b$ | $4$ |\n| $y$ | $27$ | $8$ | $1$ | $0$ | $c$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259561 1072 #uuid "04aa985e-d3c5-5600-ac7a-83a47e2753a8" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259561 1074 "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $x=4t.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=4(-1)=-4.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $x=4t.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=4(0)=0.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=1$ into $y=-{t}^{3}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=-(1)^{3}=-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-4+0+(-1)=-5.\n$$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259562 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259375 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259562 1069 "q-123763" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259562 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259562 1071 "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2\\sqrt{t+9},\\,\\,\\,y=t+1,\\,t\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nwhat is the range of $x?$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259562 1072 #uuid "2de12943-54f8-500d-9e95-bde9a205cbca" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259562 1074 "To find the range of $x,$ note that $\\sqrt{t+9}\\ge 3$ for all $t\\ge 0.$ Consequently, $x=2\\sqrt{t+9}\\ge 6.$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude that $x\\ge 6.$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259563 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259040 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259563 1069 "q-123764" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259563 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259563 1071 "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=3t-7,\\,\\,\\,y=1-t,\\,t\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nwhat is the range of $x?$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259563 1072 #uuid "808ba9b8-7fbd-5187-9780-5105c365918f" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259563 1074 "To find the range of $x,$ note that $x=3t-7\\ge -4$ for all $t\\ge 1.$ \n\nConsequently, the range of $x$ is $x\\ge -4.$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259564 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259401 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259564 1069 "q-123765" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259564 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259564 1071 "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=1-4t,\\,\\,\\,y={t}^{2}-1,\\,t\\le 0,\n$$\n\nwhat is the range of $x?$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259564 1072 #uuid "2a66d510-dc6f-5140-8b85-a40c213c087f" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259564 1074 "To find the range of $x,$ note that $x=1-4t\\ge 1$ for all $t\\le 0.$ \n\nConsequently, the range of $x$ is $x\\ge 1.$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259565 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259100 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259565 1069 "q-123767" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259565 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259565 1071 "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\,\\,y=1-t,\\,t>0,\n$$\n\nwhat is the range of $y?$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259565 1072 #uuid "e3ca4cd3-a2f5-5cf2-84dd-64e7db9e1269" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259565 1074 "To find the range of $y,$ note that $y=1-t<1$ for all $t>0.$ \n\nConsequently, the range of $y$ is $y<1.$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259566 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259426 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259566 1069 "q-123768" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259566 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259566 1071 "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=3t+2,\\,\\,\\,y=4\\sqrt{t}-1,\\,t\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nwhat is the range of $y?$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259566 1072 #uuid "a1475dc3-badf-5eaf-85a3-fd70878f8785" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259566 1074 "To find the range of $y,$ note that $4\\sqrt{t}\\ge 0$ for all $t\\ge 0.$ Consequently, $y=4\\sqrt{t}-1\\ge -1.$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude that $y\\ge -1.$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259567 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259051 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259567 1069 "q-123777" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259567 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259567 1071 "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259567 1072 #uuid "39f52df2-f7c2-52ca-a128-fe39a8ac5d3e" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259567 1074 "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -1+3 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3\\le 1+3 \\\\ 2 & \\le x\\le 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $2\\le x\\le 4.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -1-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1\\le 1-1 \\\\ -2 & \\le y\\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-2\\le y\\le 0.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $2\\le x\\le 4$ and $-2\\le y\\le 0.$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259568 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259074 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259568 1069 "q-123780" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259568 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259568 1071 "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx=t+1,\\,y=1-t,\\,-3\\le t\\le 3\n$$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259568 1072 #uuid "4690d45b-3152-570e-88c5-be7a725f4b92" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259568 1074 "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=t+1.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=1-t.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| $y$ | $4$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $-2$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](images/e8/e8cfffa1c9aaba887d90a9251a0c67402343b5a47dbb31cd85c6e648ba800e4e.png)" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259569 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259247 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259569 1069 "q-123781" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259569 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259569 1071 "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx=t-1,\\,y={t}^{2}-5,\\,-3\\le t\\le 3\n$$" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259569 1072 #uuid "4047f4e3-7a10-5d70-9b2c-847ce475f1de" 13194139533398 17592186045585 true] [17592186259569 1074 "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=t-1.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n